      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "First project-side materialization of the SOF10 frame header. The staged witness starts with `ff d8 ff ca`, so `get_sof(..., TRUE, TRUE)` marks the source JPEG as progressive arithmetic and reads the frame precision, dimensions, and component count that the arithmetic decode path and the later transform workspace sizing both consume."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_ac_nbits_must_not_exceed_max_coef_bits",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "jchuff.c",
      "function": "encode_one_block",
      "line": 575,
      "operands": [
        "nbits",
        "MAX_COEF_BITS"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "le",
        "left": "nbits",
        "right": "MAX_COEF_BITS"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_ac_nbits_within_max_coef_bits",
      "fine_trace_step": 13,
      "description": "Root cause. The vulnerable C Huffman encoder computes the bit width of a nonzero AC coefficient from the rotated destination block but never checks that the width stays within `MAX_COEF_BITS` before combining it with the zero run into a Huffman symbol index. For the witnessed transformed coefficient, this missing guard lets `nbits` reach 16 and eventually yields symbol 256."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_huffman_lookup_uses_overflowed_symbol_index",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "jchuff.c",
      "function": "encode_one_block",
      "line": 584,
      "operands": [
        "temp3"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "temp3",
        "right": "temp3"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_overflowed_symbol_index_reaches_huffman_lookup",
      "fine_trace_step": 16,
      "description": "MSAN sink. Once the derived AC symbol for the rotated destination block becomes 256, this read indexes one byte past the 256-entry `ehufsi` table and consumes adjacent image-pool bytes that were never initialized as table data."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_ac_symbol_index_hits_ehufsi_limit",
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_ac_symbol_index_hits_ehufsi_limit",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "jchuff.c",
      "function": "encode_one_block",
      "line": 582,
      "fine_trace_step": 15,
      "state": "At the AC symbol-index computation, the derived symbol index equals the 256-entry `ehufsi` table extent itself (`temp3 == sizeof (actbl->ehufsi) / sizeof (actbl->ehufsi[0])`), which is the first out-of-range lookup index.",
      "operands": [
        "sizeof (actbl->ehufsi) / sizeof (actbl->ehufsi[0])",
        "temp3"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "sizeof (actbl->ehufsi) / sizeof (actbl->ehufsi[0])",
        "right": "temp3"
      }
    }
  ],
